<title>UK: Vietnam joins International Coffee Organization.</title>
<headline>Vietnam joins International Coffee Organization.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vietnam joined the London-based International Coffee Organization (ICO), raising the membership to 60 countries, the ICO said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;I received a notification yesterday from the United Nations that the Socialist Republic of Vietnam deposited an instrument of accession to the International Coffee Agreement 1994 on 14 October 1996,&quot; executive director Celsius Lodder said.</p>
<p>Vietnam exported some 3.5 million 60-kg bags of coffee in 1995, making it the world's six biggest exporter.</p>
<p>Exporting members of the ICO now account for nearly 95 percent of global exports of coffee, Lodder said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8072</p>
